        <definition>int sl_oc::tools::StereoSgbmPar::P2</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>P2</name>
        <briefdescription>
<para>[default: 4*PI]The second parameter controlling the disparity smoothness. The larger the values are, the smoother the disparity is. P1 is the penalty on the disparity change by plus or minus 1 between neighbor pixels. P2 is the penalty on the disparity change by more than 1 between neighbor pixels. The algorithm requires P2 &gt; P1 . See stereo_match.cpp sample where some reasonably good P1 and P2 values are shown (like 8*number_of_image_channels*blockSize*blockSize and 32*number_of_image_channels*blockSize*blockSize , respectively). </para>
        </briefdescription>
